// examples/core-drift: M1's first end-to-end demonstration (see the design
// brief and gate3-decisions-and-plan.md, "M1 implementation plan" step 6) --
// ahead of `src/report`/`src/cmd` landing (M1 step 7), this package proves
// `ingest`+`compare` alone already reproduce a real, externally-observed
// compatibility change, via `core_drift_wbtest.mbt`. See PROVENANCE.md for
// where the two vendored `.mbti` files in this directory came from.
//
// This package has no real (non-test) `.mbt` file of its own yet -- it is
// the test -- so `ingest`/`compare` are only ever used from
// `core_drift_wbtest.mbt`. Scoped to `for "wbtest"` (same idiom as
// `src/ingest/moon.pkg`) rather than the main import block, which otherwise
// triggers `[0029] unused_package` since nothing in the (nonexistent) real
// code path uses them.
import {
  "mbti-compat/src/ingest",
  "mbti-compat/src/compare",
} for "wbtest"
